  "is_sufficient": false,
  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The current workflow already includes same-tensor readout checks. The proposal should identify what mutation calibration adds and obtain fresh results before treating historical failures as an unresolved current defect.",
    "Mutation eligibility and detection need independent references. If both paths share a faulty wrapper, agreement can conceal the injected fault. Specify injection locations, affected checks, detection denominators and restoration checks.",
    "Temporal prerequisites remain ambiguous: define which failures block state, score or ranking measurements, and whether missing exported-predictor coverage blocks internal sensitivity analysis.",
    "Reproduction requires fixed fixture counts and selection rules, wrapper specifications, candidate permutations, and runtime limits. The previous subprocess failure supplies no underlying exception, so its implementation cause remains unknown.",
    "Originality 4 is reasonable; potential 8 needs stronger justification given existing audit coverage and no measured recommendation improvement. Difficulty 3 appears optimistic for independent mutation calibration, adapter handling and reliable state restoration.",
    "The resumed temporal panel needs an explicit frozen specification. Earlier proposals sample training target indices, while the current workflow uses final training interactions; these define different diagnostic populations."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Establish independent mutation oracles and avoid overstating coverage from a few hand-selected faults.",
      "query": "In neural-network mutation testing, including DeepMutation and subsequent work, how are equivalent mutants, independent test oracles, mutation-score denominators and test-suite overfitting handled? Apply these principles to a fixed GRU4Rec checkpoint with temporary wrong-readout, user-row-swap and candidate-ID-permutation faults."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Determine the proposal's incremental contribution and define precise execution prerequisites.",
      "query": "What metamorphic tests and independent reference checks distinguish readout-index defects from floating-point batching differences in PyTorch unidirectional GRUs using packed variable-length histories? Consider left-padded inputs, empty rows, same-tensor final-output selection, packed-sequence row restoration and exported candidate-score parity."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Make the temporal experiment reproducible and separate user uncertainty from permutation noise.",
      "query": "How should paired permutation-sensitivity experiments for sequential recommenders estimate uncertainty when each user has five full-history shuffles and five final-item-fixed prefix shuffles? Address repeated item IDs, identity permutations, fixed candidates, user-level bootstrap versus permutation Monte Carlo error, and equal-weight aggregation across four dataset categories."
    }
  ]
}
